10. Do not use only vector similarity
This is one of the flaws we fixed.

A similar error doesn't necessarily mean a similar root cause.

For example:

"Database timeout"
could mean:

network issue
slow query
connection pool exhaustion
deadlock
overloaded DB
DNS problem
Therefore your Incident Matching Agent considers:

Error message
Stack trace
Affected service
Code path
Dependencies
Architecture
Database
Runtime context
Recent changes
Historical root cause
Then:

Case Similarity =

semantic similarity
+
service similarity
+
dependency similarity
+
architecture similarity
+
error signature similarity
+
historical context
