66. Final positioning
I would describe the product this way:

LEGACYGUARD
A Living Engineering Memory & Incident Resolution Harness

LEGACYGUARD continuously reconstructs and maintains the knowledge surrounding software systems—from code, architecture, APIs, tests, requirements and documentation to historical incidents, engineering decisions and relevant expertise. When a new failure occurs, a multi-agent harness first searches verified internal memory, falls back to external technical evidence when necessary, validates proposed solutions against the current system, challenges its own reasoning, and escalates uncertain or high-risk cases to the appropriate engineer. Once the incident is resolved, the verified outcome becomes part of the company's permanent engineering memory.

And the strongest line:

“CodeWiki explains your code. LEGACYGUARD remembers what your organization learned from it.”

